      ⍝ ----------------------------------

      2⋆70
1.180591621E21

      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, LanguageVariances.md #12, 2026-08-10):
      ⍝ UCS_string::from_big() extracted decimal digits one at a time via
      ⍝ modf(value/10.0,...) plus a "+.02" rounding fudge factor, which
      ⍝ accumulated error over many digits -- 2⋆70 is exactly
      ⍝ representable as a double (a single-bit power of 2), but this
      ⍝ lost its last few decimal digits regardless. Fixed by splitting
      ⍝ integer/fractional parts with modf() (exact, no decimal
      ⍝ rounding) and formatting the now-whole-number integer part with
      ⍝ libc's own correctly-rounded %.0f, the same fix idea as #39's.
      ⍝ Expected value independently verified via Python's exact integer
      ⍝ arithmetic (2**70), not just "what GNU APL used to print".
      ⍝
      22 0⍕2⋆70
1180591620717411303424

