      ⍝ Bugs28 #44 regression: dyadic ⍕ took every cell's real value as
      ⍝ an APL_Float up front, so a 64-bit IntCell whose magnitude
      ⍝ exceeds a double's 53-bit mantissa lost its low digits before
      ⍝ formatting even began. Fixed in Bif_F12_FORMAT.cc: an exact
      ⍝ IntCell is now formatted directly from its int64 value (via the
      ⍝ new UCS_string::from_int_to_fixed()) instead of being routed
      ⍝ through format_float_by_spec()'s APL_Float-based formatter.
      ⍝
      ]FILE_CTL SKIP_APL2   ⍝ 64-bit integers (IBM APL2: 32 bit)
