      ⍝ Bugs28 #45 regression (Bugs27 #44 residual): dyadic ⍕'s
      ⍝ fraction-digit extraction (v=v*10.0; vv=int(v); v-=vv, in
      ⍝ UCS_string::from_double_to_fixed()) accumulated one rounding
      ⍝ error PER DIGIT -- e.g. 0.15's true double value is
      ⍝ 0.14999999999999999444..., but multiplying it by 10.0 already
      ⍝ rounds UP to exactly 1.5 in the very first step, giving .2
      ⍝ instead of the correctly-rounded .1. Fixed by extracting
      ⍝ fraction digits via snprintf("%.*f", ...) instead (which works
      ⍝ from the double's exact bit pattern, like the already-fixed
      ⍝ from_big()/monadic-⍕ paths), with an explicit genuine-exact-tie
      ⍝ detection (many extra digits, check for a literal '5' followed
      ⍝ by nothing but '0's) to keep the existing round-AWAY-from-zero
      ⍝ convention for ties that glibc's own round-to-even would
      ⍝ otherwise disagree with.
      ⍝
